1
00:00:02,338 --> 00:00:10,840
Forex Desk
Genesis Forex: from a client's FX profile to a booked deal — quotes, forwards and rate alerts.

2
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:13,040
Le Morne Resorts Ltd, a hotel group, earns euros and pays its costs in rupees
It wants to sell its euro receipts forward — first, an FX profile

3
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:18,600
Sign in as Deepak Mungur — Forex Dealer
Forex dealer — quotes, books deals, manages forwards and alerts

4
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:21,640
Forex Desk ▸ FX Client Profiles: one profile per FX client
Purpose, volumes, currency pairs, approved products and limits

5
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:31,640
“Forex client onboarding” opens a two-step wizard
The FX need, then products and limits

6
00:00:31,640 --> 00:00:39,440
Approved products and the settlement limit
The limit is checked against the open forwards — the utilisation is calculated

7
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:42,160
Profile created
Its deals, open forwards and limit utilisation will build up here

8
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:54,560
The client calls: sell EUR 300,000 forward, in six weeks
FX Quotes ▸ New — client, profile, product, side, currency, amount

9
00:00:54,560 --> 00:00:59,280
“Requested at” is stamped with the time of the call
The quote timer starts from it — best execution

10
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:04,840
The FX quote timer: answer within 15 business minutes
Tools ▸ SLA Board · it counts business hours only, so a weekend request is due Monday

11
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:11,560
FX Quotes on the pipeline board
Requested ▸ Quoted ▸ Accepted / Rejected / Expired

12
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:15,120
Move the quote to Quoted…
before entering a rate

13
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:19,680
Blocked: a quote needs the quoted rate and the time it was given
No rate, no quote — the audit trail stays complete

14
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:33,520
The board buys EUR at 52.64 — Deepak quotes the client 52.90
Enter the quoted rate and the time

15
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:35,920
Quoted — the first-response timer is met
The improvement on the board rate is calculated on the quote

16
00:01:35,920 --> 00:01:39,560
The client agrees to the rate
Move the quote to Accepted

17
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:57,320
Blocked: record when the client responded
The time-stamped trail: requested → quoted → client response

18
00:01:57,320 --> 00:01:59,840
Accepted: the CRM books the deal for you
An FX deal is created and sent to the dealing system

19
00:01:59,880 --> 00:02:03,040
Forex Desk ▸ FX Deals: the deal booked from the quote
FXD-2026-000105 — forward, EUR 300,000 at 52.90

20
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:07,400
The dealing system's reference is recorded on the deal
Booked automatically when the deal was created

21
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:12,400
Board rate 52.64 · quoted 52.90 — the client gets MUR 78,000 more
Improvement against the board rate — best-execution evidence

22
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:16,760
An open forward until it settles
Days to the value date count down; the amount counts against the profile's limit

23
00:02:16,760 --> 00:02:24,080
Reminders tab: the CRM reminds the dealer a week before the value date
Confirm settlement with the client or offer a roll-over

24
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:27,560
On that day the client is also emailed and a roll-over offered
The value date shows in the dealer's calendar feed too

25
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:41,120
The client also wants to sell more euros if EUR/MUR rises to 53.60
FX Rate Alerts ▸ New — the client is told by email when the board reaches it

26
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:45,280
Active: today's board is 53.43 — below the target
Alerts are checked every hour, and whenever a new board rate is published

27
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:53,560
Next morning's board: the euro is stronger
Masters ▸ FX Reference Rates — the dealer publishes the TT buying and selling rates

28
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:56,600
The board feeds every MUR conversion, the rate alerts and the website
Save it…

29
00:02:56,600 --> 00:03:07,720
53.65 is above the client's 53.60 — the alert fires at once
The client is emailed, the alert closed as Triggered, the dealer notified

30
00:03:07,720 --> 00:03:10,240
The email to the client is on the alert's timeline
Sent in the client's language (French here) — SMS when the client prefers it

31
00:03:13,840 --> 00:03:18,360
Deepak is notified to call the client and deal
Notifications bell

32
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:30,880
The Forex Desk dashboard
Deals, volume, spread income and open forwards

33
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:36,640
Volume by currency and by month, top clients
Quote outcomes and rate alerts

34
00:03:37,571 --> 00:03:45,079
Forex Desk
The dealer quotes and decides — the CRM keeps the trail, books and reminds.
